WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.041
Meet RaahiSense.

2
00:00:01.041 --> 00:00:02.472
Raahi means traveller.

3
00:00:02.472 --> 00:00:07.900
It is a free phone app for people who are legally blind or have low vision.

4
00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:14.978
According to the World Health Organization, at least 2.2 billion people worldwide have a near or distance vision impairment.

5
00:00:14.978 --> 00:00:19.620
On busy streets, potholes, open drains and traffic make every walk risky.

6
00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:25.777
RaahiSense uses the phone's camera and on-device AI to spot obstacles and speak a warning out loud.

7
00:00:25.777 --> 00:00:28.752
For example: pothole ahead, very close.

8
00:00:28.752 --> 00:00:36.146
Carry it hands-free in a shirt pocket, with the camera facing forward and peeking over the top, or simply hold it in your hand while you walk.

9
00:00:36.146 --> 00:00:43.173
Every warning tells you the direction, left, ahead or right, and how close it is: very close, near, or far.

10
00:00:43.173 --> 00:00:50.341
It is trained on tens of thousands of images of real street obstacles, from potholes and open drains to auto-rickshaws and cows.

11
00:00:50.341 --> 00:00:52.309
RaahiSense helps at home, too.

12
00:00:52.309 --> 00:01:00.926
It warns about chairs, tables, sofas and beds, stairs, and people or pets in the way, so moving around the house is easier.

13
00:01:00.926 --> 00:01:06.856
It works fully offline, with no Wi-Fi or mobile data, on low-cost, everyday Android phones.

14
00:01:06.856 --> 00:01:09.768
So it fits places where connectivity is patchy.

15
00:01:09.768 --> 00:01:11.190
Control is hands-free.

16
00:01:11.190 --> 00:01:18.204
Just say, Hey Guide, then a command like: what's in front of me, repeat, louder, or change language.

17
00:01:18.204 --> 00:01:24.610
On noisy streets, simply long-press a volume key, double-tap anywhere on the screen, or shake the phone.

18
00:01:24.610 --> 00:01:32.153
It keeps running with the screen off in your pocket or bag, speaks warnings in multiple languages starting with English, and it is completely free.

19
00:01:32.153 --> 00:01:34.240
And RaahiSense keeps getting smarter.

20
00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:40.600
As more people use it, it learns from real streets and homes, with sharing always optional and private.

21
00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:47.511
Coming next: a standalone RaahiSense device with a small camera that clips onto your shirt, so no smartphone is needed.

22
00:01:47.511 --> 00:01:48.501
RaahiSense.

23
00:01:48.501 --> 00:01:51.112
Safer steps, spoken out loud.

24
00:01:51.112 --> 00:01:54.263
A project by Dr. Chindanoor Rajesh.

25
00:01:54.263 --> 00:02:00.305
Visit raahisense.com, or reach us at raahisenseapp@gmail.com.
